-------------------------------------------------------------------------
A note on the inherited code
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

WW-DHSVM is a fork of Watershed Workflow, which is distributed under the
3-clause BSD licence.  The MIT terms above cover WW-DHSVM's own work.  The
portions inherited from Watershed Workflow -- most of ww_dhsvm/sources/,
together with crs.py, warp.py, colors.py and their companions -- remain
under their original 3-clause BSD licence, reproduced verbatim in
LICENSE.watershed-workflow.

Both licences are permissive and compatible; in practice this means you may
use, modify and redistribute the whole of this repository freely, provided
you keep both notices.  The one obligation MIT does not carry on its own is
BSD's third clause: do not use the names of the national laboratories or
their contributors to endorse products derived from the inherited code.
